# GasBrineBench -- DENY BY DEFAULT.
#
# This repository is public, and it is developed inside a working tree that
# also holds 884 MB of publisher PDFs, unpublished collaborator manuscripts,
# reviewer correspondence and .tex sources. None of that may ever be
# committed. A conventional ignore list cannot guarantee that: it enumerates
# what to exclude, so anything nobody thought of gets committed by the next
# `git add -A`.
#
# So nothing here is trackable unless it is named below. Adding a new kind of
# file to this repository is a deliberate act that has to be written into this
# file first.
#
# To check the allowlist after editing:
#     git add -A --dry-run          # must list only intended files
#     git status --short            # must be clean after a commit
#     git check-ignore -v <path>    # shows which rule decided a given path

*

# Let git descend into directories at all; the rules below decide the files.
!*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation and repository metadata (root only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!/README.md
!/SCHEMA.md
!/LEDGER.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/LICENSE
!/CITATION.cff
!/SOURCES.md
!/SOURCES.bib
!/.gitignore
!/.github/workflows/*.yml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The database and its documentation
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!/data/*.csv
!/data/README.md
!/data/QUALITY.md

# The hand-maintained bibliographic library that SOURCES.* is generated from.
!/bib/references.bib

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Code: the validator, the manifest generator, and the build scripts kept as
# provenance documentation.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!/tools/*.py
!/tools/builders/*.py
!/tools/builders/README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The raw hand transcriptions. Only files named EXP*.txt, only under
# transcriptions/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!/transcriptions/README.md
!/transcriptions/MANIFEST.tsv
!/transcriptions/**/EXP*.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Belt and braces. These come last, so they override every re-admission above:
# no rule added later can let one of them in by accident.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Directory names that only ever appear in the non-redistributable trove.
source_materials/
source_data/
papers/
paper/
manuscript*/
drafts/
reviews/
correspondence/
emails/

# Solver-output trees in the source trove. Their files are named EXP*.txt too,
# so the transcriptions allowlist above would otherwise admit them; the
# extraction rule excludes them for the same reason (see
# tools/extract_transcriptions.py).
OPT*/
TXT/

# Publisher content, manuscripts, and private correspondence.
*.pdf
*.ps
*.eps
*.djvu
*.tex
*.bbl
*.doc
*.docx
*.odt
*.rtf
*.pptx
*.eml
*.mbox

# Bulk and binary artefacts: regenerable, and nothing here should be large.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.tif
*.tiff
*.parquet
*.dat
*.npz
*.npy
*.mat
*.sav
*.h5
*.zip
*.tar
*.gz
*.7z
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.a
*.exe
*.whl
*.pyc

# Interpreter, editor and OS droppings.
__pycache__/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.env
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
*.bak
*.log
